    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d92">

                <pb facs="0219" n="193" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v19/pg193"/>

                <head>92. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Afghanistan<anchor n="0" xml:id="d92-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-01-12T22:56:00-05:00">January 12, 1962,
                            10:56 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>256. Eyes Only Ambassador. President, who considered transit trade impasse
                    January 11, desires USG should continue maximum
                    efforts to assist resolution this dispute. He is agreeable using some funds meet
                    commitment in US draft note to Afghans re utilization Iranian route. However in
                    view fact Afghans have capability of permitting entry aid goods via cheaper
                    traditional route, President is opposed to use of Iranian route at added costs
                    over extended period.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d92-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d92-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 689.9OD/1-1262. Secret; Niact.
                    Drafted by Talbot and Weil; cleared by Hewitt, Gaud, and McGeorge
                        Bundy; and approved by Rusk. Repeated to Karachi and Tehran.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
